    {
      "id": "HNT-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-cyclic-tate-vanishing",
      "title": "Fundamental equality and Tate cohomology vanishing for cyclic idèle class groups",
      "hypotheses": "Number fields K and L with L/K a finite Galois extension whose Galois group G = Gal(L/K) is cyclic with generator σ; idèle class groups C_K = 𝕀_K / K^× and C_L = 𝕀_L / L^×, base-change embedding ι : C_K ↪ C_L, idèle class norm N_{L/K} : C_L → C_K, cyclic Tate cohomology groups Ĥ⁰(G, C_L) = C_L^G / N_G(C_L) and Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L) = ker(N_G) / (σ − 1)C_L, Herbrand quotient h(C_L) = [L : K], and the second inequality [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)] ≤ [L : K].",
      "statement": "The base-change map induces an isomorphism C_K / N_{L/K}(C_L) ≅ Ĥ⁰(G, C_L), whence [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)] = [L : K] · |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| with |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| ≥ 1, giving the first inequality [L : K] ≤ [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)]. Combining with the second inequality [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)] ≤ [L : K] yields the fundamental equality [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)] = [L : K], and cancelling [L : K] > 0 establishes the class-field axiom for cyclic idèle classes: |Ĥ⁰(G, C_L)| = [L : K] and |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| = 1. In particular, every idèle class c ∈ C_L with N_G(c) = 1 has the form σ(d)/d for some d ∈ C_L.",
      "definitions": [
        "cyclic Tate cohomology groups Ĥ⁰(G, C_L) = ker(σ − 1) / im(N_G) and Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L) = ker(N_G) / im(σ − 1) for a generator σ of G = Gal(L/K)",
        "Herbrand quotient h(C_L) = |Ĥ⁰(G, C_L)| / |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| = [L : K] with finite numerator and denominator",
        "fundamental equality [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)] = [L : K] and class-field axiom (|Ĥ⁰(G, C_L)| = [L : K], |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| = 1)"
      ],
