      "status": "source checked",
      "correspondence": "The base-change homomorphism ι : C_K → C_L is injective with image C_L^G = ker(σ − 1) and intertwines the idèle-class norm N_{L/K} with the cyclic Galois norm N_G = ∏_{g∈G} g, giving C_K / N_{L/K}(C_L) ≅ Ĥ⁰(G, C_L). Substituting |Ĥ⁰(G, C_L)| = [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)] into the Herbrand quotient h(C_L) = [L : K] gives [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)] = [L : K] · |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| and the first inequality; antisymmetry with the second inequality forces [C_K : N_{L/K}(C_L)] = [L : K] and hence |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| = 1.",
      "review": "Checked surjectivity onto C_L^G via Galois invariants of idèle classes, kernel identification via injectivity of base change and N_G = ι ∘ N_{L/K}, finiteness/positivity of |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| from the Herbrand quotient, antisymmetry between the first and second inequalities, and left cancellation of [L : K] > 0."
    },
