      "id": "HNT-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-quadratic-hasse-norm",
      "title": "Cyclic and quadratic Hasse norm theorems and everywhere-local norm criteria for CM ideals",
      "hypotheses": "Number fields K and L with L/K a finite cyclic Galois extension (in particular any quadratic extension [L : K] = 2), x ∈ K^×, and the vanishing |Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_L)| = 1 from HNT-01; for the CM criteria, a CM number field K with maximal real subfield K^+, complex conjugation c, finite unramifiedness of K/K^+ at every finite place, a nonzero integral ideal I ⊆ 𝒪_K, an algebraic integer a ∈ 𝒪_K with I · c(I) = (a), x ∈ (K^+)^× mapping to a in K, and total positivity Re φ(a) > 0 for every complex embedding φ : K → ℂ.",
      "statement": "For any cyclic Galois extension L/K of number fields (and in particular any quadratic extension [L : K] = 2), an element x ∈ K^× lies in N_{L/K}(L^×) if and only if its diagonal idèle diag(x) lies in N_{L/K}(𝕀_L), which holds if and only if x is a local norm at every finite place v and every infinite place v of K. For a CM field K unramified over K^+ at all finite places, if a nonzero ideal I ⊆ 𝒪_K satisfies I · c(I) = (a) where a = x ∈ (K^+)^× is totally positive (Re φ(a) > 0 for all φ : K → ℂ), then x is a local norm at every finite place and every infinite place of K^+, and hence x = N_{K/K^+}(β) for some β ∈ K^×.",
      "definitions": [
        "diagonal embedding diag : K^× ↪ 𝕀_K and idèle norm N_{L/K} : 𝕀_L → 𝕀_K with finite and infinite local components",
        "Dedekind approximation b ∈ I with I P + (b) = I for P = v 𝒪_K, yielding (b) = I J, b c(b) = a t, and t ∉ w for every prime w over v",
        "local archimedean d-th root r = e⁻¹(e(x)^{1/d}) ∈ K^+_v (d = [K_W : K^+_v] ∈ {1, 2}) witnessing x as a local norm at each real place v of K^+"
      ],
